# baseline used to grade your work.  Its intent to offer you some flexibility in choosing your style.  If, for example, you can’t
# live with the Allman brace style, you may pick another brace style by setting the BreakBeforeBraces option to something else, say
# Attach.  For a complete set of options to tweak, see Clang-Format Style Options.
#
# That said, there is nothing you need to do.  Simply submit _clang_format unchanged with all your other files.  But if you do want
# to be graded against a different style, submit your modified _clang_format file.  Keep in mind that no tool will ever be able to
# format your code perfectly.  Formatting tools are a starting point.  Ultimately, you the human must ensure your code is of high
# quality, readable, and maintainable.
#
# See Clang-Format Style Options @ https://releases.llvm.org/22.1.0/tools/clang/docs/ClangFormatStyleOptions.html


